BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
CASE NO: W.P. No. 22340 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC010891232026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice Mohammed Shaffiq

PARTIES:
M/s Precision Auto Components Private Limited
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Assistant Commissioner of State Tax, Large Taxpayers Unit, Chennai
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Central Goods and Services Tax Act 2017, Tamil Nadu Goods and Services Tax Act 2017

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
CGST Act Section 16\(2\)\(c\), CGST Act Section 16\(4\), TNGST Act Section 16

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
GST Input Tax Credit, Bona Fide Purchaser, Supplier Default, GSTR-2A Matching, Tax Invoice

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Revenue reversed petitioner's Input Tax Credit on grounds that selling dealer failed to remit collected tax into government treasury.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Can genuine purchasing dealer who holds valid tax invoice and bank payment proofs be denied ITC for vendor's non-remittance?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Where purchasing dealer proves bona fide purchase with invoice and banking channel proof, ITC cannot be denied without proceeding against defaulting supplier first.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; Input Tax Credit denial quashed; Purchasing dealer cannot be penalized for supplier default.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice Mohammed Shaffiq
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
